-- title:
--   Relative group law on the projective Weierstrass model over a Noetherian domain
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian integral domain (a commutative ring that is a domain and Noetherian) and let $V$ be a projective Weierstrass curve over $R$ whose associated affine Weierstrass curve is elliptic, i.e. has invertible discriminant. Write $E = \mathrm{Proj}$ of the grading `projModelGradingCR V`, the quotient of the polynomial ring in three variables over $R$, with its standard grading, by the homogeneous ideal generated by the Weierstrass cubic of $V$, and let `projModelStrCR V` be the structure morphism $E \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ obtained as `Proj.toSpecZero` followed by the morphism of spectra induced by $R \to (\text{degree-}0\text{ part})$. Assume further that for every field $K$ equipped with an $R$-algebra structure (in the same universe) there exists an isomorphism of schemes between the pullback of `projModelStrCR V` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $R \to K$ and the corresponding projective model `projModelCR` of the base change $V_K$. The conclusion is that the type `RelativeGroupLaw R (projModelStrCR V)` is nonempty: there is a structure assigning, to every scheme $T$ with a morphism $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} R$, a multiplication, a unit element and an inversion on the set of morphisms $\varphi : T \to E$ with $\varphi$ followed by the structure morphism equal to $t$, such that multiplication is associative, the unit is a two-sided identity, inversion is a left inverse, and multiplication commutes with precomposition along any $\psi : T' \to T$ with $\psi$ followed by $t$ equal to $t'$. No commutativity of the multiplication is asserted.
--
--   This is the group-law axiom package for the projective Weierstrass model of an elliptic curve over a base, in the functor-of-points form: the $T$-points of $E$ over $\operatorname{Spec} R$ form a group, functorially in $T$. It is the input to the refinement [`WeierstrassProjModel.exists_relativeGroupLaw_isCommutative_one_eq_zeroSect_of_isElliptic_of_baseChangeIso`](thm.html#WeierstrassProjModel.exists_relativeGroupLaw_isCommutative_one_eq_zeroSect_of_isElliptic_of_baseChangeIso), where the law is additionally shown to be commutative with unit the zero section, and it belongs to the construction of the scheme-theoretic group structure used in the Néron-model infrastructure.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassProjModel_relativeGroupLaw_nonempty_of_isElliptic_of_baseChangeIso_of_isNoetherianRing.lean

import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassCurve_ProjModel
import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.EllipticCurve.Affine.Point
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Noetherian.Defs

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits NeronModelInfra WeierstrassProjModel

universe u

theorem WeierstrassProjModel.relativeGroupLaw_nonempty_of_isElliptic_of_baseChangeIso_of_isNoetherianRing
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    (V : WeierstrassCurve.Projective R)
    [V.toAffine.IsElliptic]
    (hbc : ∀ (K : Type u) [Field K] [Algebra R K],
        Nonempty (pullback (projModelStrCR V)
            (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R K)))
          ≅ projModelCR (V.baseChange K))) :
    Nonempty (RelativeGroupLaw R (projModelStrCR V)) := by sorry
